[COMMENTS]
STATION,Twin Laserflow Index Velocity gauges from 01/10/2022, replacing multipath ultrasonic time-of-flight gauge. River splits flows through two rectangular flood drainage channels. GENERAL: Two rectangular concrete flood drainage channels, each 3.9m wide, 3.09m deep, separated by divide wall 1m high. Informal low flow controls installed 1981; closed 1984, reopened 1991 as multipath ultrasonic gauge, replaced with Laserflow index velocity gauge in 2022. STATION HYDROMETRY: No ratings available. Unstable ratings in early record. Somewhat improved following installation of informal low flow controls in 1981. Closed 1984, reopened 1991 as a multipath ultrasonic operation. Stop boards can close one channel at low flows. All flows contained. FLOW RECORD: Pre-1972 the data is from CEH data holdings. Between 1972 and 1992 the data is the sum of the flows from the left (4027) and right (4227) channels. Summary and daily mean flow data available for this period. Use with care (especially low flows) due to unstable ratings. Informal low flow controls improved data somewhat from 1981. Closed 1984. 15min data available from 1991 when the site reopened as a multipath ultrasonic operation, continues with data from Laserflow Index Velocity gauge from 2022. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in August 2025 (WINFAP Files v14). FLOW REGIME: Substantial augmentation from mine drainage and mining towns' STW. Runoff influenced by groundwater abstraction/recharge. Runoff increased by effluent returns. Runoff reduced by industrial/agricultural abstraction. Substantial mining in catchment.
CATCHMENT,Low to moderate relief catchment draining Carboniferous Coal Measures with Permian and Triassic rocks on east and south boundaries. Significant urban fraction, otherwise arable and grazing land use.
Qmed Suitability,Gauged above QMED. All flows contained and ultrasonic appears to perform well.
Pooling Suitability,Gauged to within 2% of AMAX3. All flows contained and ultrasonic appears to perform well.
[END]
